  {"id":90,"x":620,"y":180,"z":0,"title":"Velaka Desert","descriptions":["A wide valley between two mountains of unrelenting sand curves at a graceful arc between the peaks.  To one side stands the gentle back slope of a dune, a simple yet tedious trek toward the apex, while opposite towers an imposing slip face, a short and exhausting climb.  Between the two heights stretches a wedge of sky, bringing with it all the independent challenges of the Velakan day.","The landscape of Velaka stretches out below the peak of this mountain of fine sand.  Sloping gently but acutely away from the towering height, only to rise again and again toward the horizon, an expansive field of crescent-shaped dunes crawls at a generational pace through the desert.  Tiny trails ascend and descend the slip face on the concave side of the dune, evidence of whatever strange life thrives in this harsh world.","A low point stands between two great dune fields, separated by an arm of tall, jagged stones.  Eastward stands an expansive sprawl of crescent-shaped dunes, the wide hills of blowing sand stretching out toward the far horizon.  West beyond the stones, relatively calmer winds prevail, forming low mounds that roll to and fro.","This low point, nestled comfortably between the silhouettes of two oppressive sand dunes, offers superficial shelter from the wind carried by overhead.  While from one perspective the valley serves to protect its inhabitants, the reality that escape through the shifting sand will be an arduous task looms ominously, hinted at by the distant slice of sky visible between the peaks.","Under a cold and uncaring sky, the pale and ghostly sand of the Velakan night sprawls in every direction.  From this vantage point atop one of the massive, crescent-shaped dunes, the typically lifeless landscape of the desert becomes somehow more desolate and ominous.  At least a full league from peak to peak, each dune stands alone in the darkness, exposed and silent in its sunless vigil, offering no shelter or comfort to lost travelers."],"exits":[{"to":89,"exit":"north","move":"rt north","hidden":true},{"to":89,"exit":"northeast","move":"rt northeast","hidden":true},{"to":91,"exit":"east","move":"rt east"},{"to":91,"exit":"southeast","move":"rt southeast","hidden":true},{"to":91,"exit":"south","move":"rt south","hidden":true},{"to":91,"exit":"southwest","move":"rt southwest","hidden":true},{"to":89,"exit":"west","move":"rt west","hidden":true},{"to":89,"exit":"northwest","move":"rt northwest"}]},
  {"id":91,"x":640,"y":180,"z":0,"title":"Velaka Desert, Beneath the Dry Dock","descriptions":["To the west, the barren landscape of the Velaka Desert takes on the appearance of a painting, framed on the top and sides by the aged wood of the dry dock and its supports.  A seemingly endless sea of crescent-shaped dunes stretches forth, blocking the horizon almost immediately from view.  The dock itself stands partially submerged in the base of the first slope, a lone scout of an ever-encroaching army of sand."],"exits":[{"to":90,"exit":"north","move":"rt north","hidden":true},{"to":90,"exit":"west","move":"rt west"},{"to":90,"exit":"northwest","move":"rt northwest","hidden":true},{"to":92,"exit":"climb","move":"climb frayed rope"}]},
  {"id":92,"x":660,"y":180,"z":0,"title":"Hvaral, Dry Dock","descriptions":["A dock extends from the stone roadway here, hanging out over a low-lying mountain road.  No water here, and certainly no ships, Hvaral's Dry Dock is serviced by barges pulled by somewhat strange looking beasts.  Outside the protection of the wall, arid mountain winds sting the faces of those who would dare to tarry in the open.  Officials in Therengia's blue and gold livery thoroughly inspect rows of crates and barrels that litter the dock, awaiting either import or export.  ","A dock extends from the stone roadway here, hanging out over a low-lying mountain road.  No water here, and certainly no ships, Hvaral's Dry Dock is serviced by barges pulled by somewhat strange looking beasts.  Outside the protection of the wall, arid mountain winds sting the faces of those who would dare to tarry in the open.  Officials in Therengia's blue and gold livery thoroughly inspect rows of crates and barrels that litter the dock, awaiting either import or export."],"exits":[{"to":0,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":91,"exit":"climb","move":"climb frayed rope"}],"aliases":["Dry Dock"],"linksTo":"Map41_Marauders.xml"},
  {"id":93,"x":200,"y":-120,"z":0,"title":"Velaka Desert","descriptions":["About halfway up one of the massive arms of a huge, star-shaped dune, the landscape of the desert becomes slightly more apparent.  Stretching out in all directions further than the eye can see, great sandy mountains are the only decoration on an endless canvas of blowing amber grains, shifting about on a generational timescale.  Many of the peaks rise not much higher than this vantage point, though several lift daringly into the sky, as if challenging the desert wind to obliterate them.","This low valley surrounded on all sides by immense, star-shaped dunes is just one of many locations within the expansive Velaka Desert that a hapless wanderer could be forgotten for eternity.  No sign of the horizon can be found from the bottom of this basin, edged in on all sides by almost insurmountable walls of loose sand, shifting in the slightest breeze yet refusing to give way.  The broad swath of sky overhead only reinforces the image of a hopelessly deep trough in an ocean of sand.","Nearing the midsection of this massive arm which radiates outward from the center of an enormous star-shaped dune, the Velaka Desert stands solemnly desolate under the cover of night.  Though the sandy mountain is one in a sea of similar shapes stretching as far as the eye can see, cast in the shadow of darkness it manages to retain a solitary appearance.  Still, several peaks rise yet higher into the air, as if challenging the wind to obliterate them before morning.","Dark and oppressive shapes loom on all sides, the shadowy nocturnal visages of the towering star-shaped dunes which dominate this portion of the Velaka Desert, stoic and silent.  The horizon in every direction is blocked by the hulking mountains of sand, making navigation by landmark an impossibility, the dunes themselves changing shape in the passing wind.  Overhead, visible only over the peaks of the darkened hills, the sky serves as a reminder of the depth of the valley.","The entirety of Velaka spreads out below this colossus of sand, the tremendous height of the mountain towering over all others within sight.  From here the famous star-shaped patterns of the dune field are immediately apparent, looking much like an army of immense starfish crawling toward the mountains on the horizon out of a great ocean, leagues away.  Unlike many of the other regions of the desert, no telltale signs of life persist here, proving this as the most untouched corner of this barren land."],"exits":[{"to":94,"exit":"north","move":"rt north","hidden":true},{"to":36,"exit":"northeast","move":"rt northeast","hidden":true},{"to":36,"exit":"east","move":"rt east"},{"to":36,"exit":"southeast","move":"rt southeast","hidden":true},{"to":94,"exit":"south","move":"rt south","hidden":true},{"to":94,"exit":"southwest","move":"rt southwest","hidden":true},{"to":94,"exit":"west","move":"rt west"},{"to":94,"exit":"northwest","move":"rt northwest","hidden":true}]},
