epth of the valley.","The entirety of Velaka spreads out below this colossus of sand, the tremendous height of the mountain towering over all others within sight.  From here the famous star-shaped patterns of the dune field are immediately apparent, looking much like an army of immense starfish crawling toward the mountains on the horizon out of a great ocean, leagues away.  Unlike many of the other regions of the desert, no telltale signs of life persist here, proving this as the most untouched corner of this barren land."],"exits":[{"to":125,"exit":"north","move":"rt north","hidden":true},{"to":125,"exit":"northeast","move":"rt northeast"},{"to":128,"exit":"east","move":"rt east","hidden":true},{"to":128,"exit":"southeast","move":"rt southeast","hidden":true},{"to":128,"exit":"south","move":"rt south","hidden":true},{"to":128,"exit":"southwest","move":"rt southwest","hidden":true},{"to":128,"exit":"west","move":"rt west"},{"to":125,"exit":"northwest","move":"rt northwest","hidden":true}]},
  {"id":128,"x":-500,"y":-20,"z":0,"title":"Velaka Desert","descriptions":["About halfway up one of the massive arms of a huge, star-shaped dune, the landscape of the desert becomes slightly more apparent.  Stretching out in all directions further than the eye can see, great sandy mountains are the only decoration on an endless canvas of blowing amber grains, shifting about on a generational timescale.  Many of the peaks rise not much higher than this vantage point, though several lift daringly into the sky, as if challenging the desert wind to obliterate them.","This low valley surrounded on all sides by immense, star-shaped dunes is just one of many locations within the expansive Velaka Desert that a hapless wanderer could be forgotten for eternity.  No sign of the horizon can be found from the bottom of this basin, edged in on all sides by almost insurmountable walls of loose sand, shifting in the slightest breeze yet refusing to give way.  The broad swath of sky overhead only reinforces the image of a hopelessly deep trough in an ocean of sand.","Nearing the midsection of this massive arm which radiates outward from the center of an enormous star-shaped dune, the Velaka Desert stands solemnly desolate under the cover of night.  Though the sandy mountain is one in a sea of similar shapes stretching as far as the eye can see, cast in the shadow of darkness it manages to retain a solitary appearance.  Still, several peaks rise yet higher into the air, as if challenging the wind to obliterate them before morning.","Dark and oppressive shapes loom on all sides, the shadowy nocturnal visages of the towering star-shaped dunes which dominate this portion of the Velaka Desert, stoic and silent.  The horizon in every direction is blocked by the hulking mountains of sand, making navigation by landmark an impossibility, the dunes themselves changing shape in the passing wind.  Overhead, visible only over the peaks of the darkened hills, the sky serves as a reminder of the depth of the valley.","The entirety of Velaka spreads out below this colossus of sand, the tremendous height of the mountain towering over all others within sight.  From here the famous star-shaped patterns of the dune field are immediately apparent, looking much like an army of immense starfish crawling toward the mountains on the horizon out of a great ocean, leagues away.  Unlike many of the other regions of the desert, no telltale signs of life persist here, proving this as the most untouched corner of this barren land."],"exits":[{"to":127,"exit":"north","move":"rt north","hidden":true},{"to":127,"exit":"northeast","move":"rt northeast","hidden":true},{"to":127,"exit":"east","move":"rt east"},{"to":129,"exit":"climb","move":"climb black stones"}]},
  {"id":129,"x":-480,"y":-120,"z":0,"title":"Velaka Desert","descriptions":["A large, flat expanse of sand stretches between two gigantic dunes here.  Rising smoothly up from the uneven ground around them, mammoth-like, they seem not to shift despite the most valiant attempts of the harsh desert wind that so often rips across this barren land.","A wide, unrelieved expanse of sand stretches out to all sides, the sky overhead untouched by any other plant or animal life.  It bears down almost oppressively overhead, indefatigable in its endless stretch in all directions.","Brief clumps of squat, sparse brush dot the hard ground below.  Only a low dusting of sand covers the space between them, for nature is ever fickle, offering no easy purchase for clinging roots when it does provide the nutrients to sustain them.","Dust rises with each footstep as the soft powdery sand, worn away by wind and erosion and grinding against the other objects, fills the air.  The dunes are miniature mountains, their massive bulks rising high into air, constantly shifting as the wind moves them about.","Heat shimmers rise over the sandy plain, blurring the air and creating silvery pools of illusion on the ground in the far distance.  The massive Gemfire heights in the east mingle with the surely false blurry sights of treetops and rainfalls.","Rolling dunes of sun-blasted sand stretch as far as the eye can see.  The sheer solitude of the area is intimidating -- not a sound can be heard save the intermittent whistle of the wind and the resultant shift of sand.  Daylight seems to pummel down from overhead, heavy and implacable.","Slabs of stone have pushed up past the surface, poking out through the skin of Velaka like horribly fractured bones.  Though large by normal standards, the formations are dwarfed by the craggy peaks of the Gemfire Mountains dominating the eastern horizon.","Sparse, tenacious weeds clump sullenly around the protective shade provided by the steep crags thrusting up from the silver desert sand.  Survivors to the core, they cling to the rock and throw their narrow, olive leaves outward as if to ward off any that would challenge their meager presence.","The sharp, sunset-banded rock of the canyon transitions here to a dark black stone.  Indicating the presence of some darker ore within, the surface shines faintly and appears to crumble easily as fist-sized chunks of it pepper the ground below, offering up dangerously sharp edges to beleaguer the unwary."],"exits":[{"to":128,"exit":"go","move":"go black stones"},{"to":0,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":0,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":0,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":0,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":0,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":0,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":0,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":0,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"linksTo":"Map47_Muspar'i.xml"}
 ],
 "labels": [
  {"text":"Cadaverous Yeehar","x":420,"y":-200,"z":0},
  {"text":"Twisting Trail","x":280,"y":-20,"z":0},
  {"text":"Slot Canyon","x":320,"y":30,"z":0},
  {"text":"Broad Valley","x":240,"y":100,"z":0},
  {"text":"Path","x":200,"y":50,"z":0},
  {"text":"shifting maze","x":210,"y":10,"z":0},
  {"text":"(shifting maze)","x":-510,"y":-140,"z":0},
  {"text":"Muspar'i","x":-495,"y":-150,"z":0},
  {"text":"Leather Repair","x":185,"y":-95,"z":0}
 ]
}
